    "title": "LESSON 5: TWO LAYERS, ONE WORD",
    "header_color": "magenta",
    "pages": [
      {
        "page": 1,
        "total_pages": 1,
        "content": [
          "English carries a Latin layer and a",
          "Greek layer side by side. Often a",
          "word is built from only one.",
          "",
          "But sometimes one word mixes both in",
          "a single build. That is a HYBRID.",
          "",
          "television: tele (Greek, far) +",
          "vision (Latin, sight).",
          "",
          "automobile: auto (Greek, self) +",
          "mobile (Latin, moving).",
          "",
          "sociology: socio (Latin, society) +",
          "-logy (Greek, study).",
          "",
          "Purists once frowned on hybrids.",
          "English kept building them anyway."
        ],
